Data   : CommandsPageViewModel binds the shared S8 VehiclesStore.vehicles() (web useVehicles) and, per vehicle,
         VehiclesStore.vehicleState(id) (web per-vehicle `command-vehicle-states` map) via commandsPageSourceOf();
         the vehicle list drives the page phase, the per-vehicle states are folded into CommandsSnapshot. Each
         embedded VehicleCommandCenter binds its own `command-latest` feed (HttpCommandsRepository.commandLatest,
         parsed to CommandLogEntry at the source boundary) + the shared VehicleCommandStore dispatcher
         (StoreCommandCenterCommander). No HTTP in the view.
Adapt  : the OpenAPI-generated `Vehicle` model carries no inline `state`/`battery_*` (the web local `Vehicle`
         type does), so online/asleep counts AND each command center's vehicle badge are sourced from the SAME
         per-vehicle `/vehicles/{id}/state` feed — one source of truth, no drift (CommandsPageModel.kt
         isVehicleOnline + toCommandCenterVehicle).
Strings: all 13 page keys already present in res/values/strings.xml (generated by apps/shared/i18n/generators/
         gen-i18n.ts) — no string-catalog edit needed; every literal resolves via stringResource(R.string.translation_*).
Nav    : Destinations 'commands' -> /commands pre-existing (Destinations.kt:167; count unchanged); host wired via
         PageHosts.register; "View History" -> /command-history opened through the app's own teslasync://app
         deep-link scheme (AndroidManifest + TeslaSyncNavHost) since no NavController is exposed to page hosts.

